From 00ada270ef5934bf7655592c354e9da2f682c2b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:16:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] VAX8200: DMB32 synchronous line (DDCMP); DMF32 sync line on
 the shared code

The DMB32's synchronous line, DDCMP only (DMB32 design D3), from the
DMB32 User Guide 3.3.28-3.3.43, 3.3.52, 3.4.6, 3.4.8, 3.4.11 and the
Technical Description 2.7:
- two transmit and two receive buffers (TBUFFADn/CTn/TLNCTRLn,
  RBUFFADn/CTn/RLNCTRLn): DMA.START, DMA.ABORT, BUFCTRL buffer priority;
- the board frames DDCMP: transmit takes header and data and adds both
  CRCs, receive stores header and data without them (bad header CRC:
  frame dropped; bad data CRC, message too long: message errors);
- completions and modem changes in SBUF, the sync interrupt;
- LPR1 receiver enable, loopback, modem change suppression, line reset;
  LPR2 modem signals, protocol, modem override; BUFCTRL shows a V.24
  cable;
- unit DMB-SYNC: SET DMB-SYNC PEER=host:port, ATTACH DMB-SYNC port, a
  DDCMP link to a DMC11/DMR11/DMP11/DMV11/DMF32/DMB32 in another
  simulator.

The link to the peer and the DDCMP framing are in vax_combo_lib.c (taken
from the DMF32's sync line), and the DMF32 sync line uses them too
(design D1, phase P4a).  The DMF32 keeps its registers, buffers,
interrupts, tributary check, HDLC/SDLC and GEN BYTE; a received DDCMP
frame with a bad start character is now dropped like one with a bad
header CRC.

Tested (tests/dmb32/p4.sh): VMS V5.5 (SIDRIVER) on the VAX 8200, DECnet
circuit DMB-0 to a MicroVAX II with a DMV11 and to a VAX-11/780 with a
DMF32, both VMS V4.7; VMS V4.7 XGDRIVER on the DMF32 of the 8200 to the
DMV11: circuits up, copies there and back with 0 differences, LOOP NODE,
SET HOST.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SuavtftJEqWTX7fajw6zWU
